# 1. PROJECT UNDERSTANDING — DO NOT CHANGE THE CORE IDEA

FairResolve is an evidence-aware, policy-grounded dispute investigation and refund resolution platform for online merchants who use PayPal.

It transforms unstructured customer complaints into structured investigations.

It combines:

1. Customer-reported information.
2. Verified PayPal transaction information.
3. Merchant-provided information.
4. Customer-submitted evidence.
5. AI-generated evidence observations.
6. Deterministic merchant refund-policy evaluation.
7. Explicit merchant authorization.
8. Actual PayPal refund execution.
9. Audit history and payment reconciliation.

## Official product statement

"FairResolve transforms unstructured customer complaints into structured, evidence-aware, policy-grounded investigations, then enables authorized merchants to make informed decisions and execute verified refunds through PayPal."

This is not another AI chatbot.

It must not become a generic CRM, helpdesk or administrative dashboard.

The main product is an operational dispute-investigation and payment-resolution system.

## Non-negotiable principle

A customer claim is not a verified fact.

An AI observation is not proof.

A policy recommendation is not merchant authorization.

A refund request is not a completed refund.

Only the merchant has authority to approve a refund, and only PayPal's actual response can establish the corresponding PayPal payment status.

