4. Frontend calls the backend capture endpoint using the returned PayPal order identifier.
5. Backend verifies the order and capture response.
6. Backend stores the real order, capture, amount and currency.
7. Backend generates a secure customer complaint link.

Never capture an order simply because the browser requested a checkout session.

Never trust browser-supplied payment amounts or status.

